@startuml BackendCurrent
title Hermes backend: accepted direction and explicit proposals
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
actor "CLI / TUI" as Client
component "document-service\nUsers / authentication\nWorkspaces / documents" as HDS
component "notification-service\nWebSocket connections\nRouting / delivery" as HNS
database "Document PostgreSQL\nProfiles / credentials\nWorkspaces / memberships / documents" as DB
database "Redis\nActive sessions" as Redis
queue "Kafka\nDomain events" as Kafka
database "Notification PostgreSQL\nDurable inbox: policy OPEN" as Inbox

Client --> HDS : Public API\nregister / login / domain operations
Client <--> HNS : WebSocket\nconnection + live messages
HDS --> DB : Own domain data
HDS --> Redis : Create / revoke sessions
HNS --> Redis : Validate session on connect
HDS --> Kafka : Domain facts\npublication reliability OPEN
Kafka --> HNS : Consume and fan out
HNS ..> Inbox : Durable notification policy OPEN

note bottom of Redis
  ACCEPTED: shared active session store (ADR-001).
  Roles belong to workspace memberships, not sessions.
  Revocation for already-open sockets remains OPEN.
end note
note bottom of HDS
  PROPOSED (ADR-003): own notification settings;
  PostgreSQL durable state -> versioned Redis representation
  -> explicit Pub/Sub UserSettingsChanged(user_id, version).
  Every HNS instance reloads settings for its local connections.
  Reconnect/resync repairs missed Pub/Sub signals.
end note
note bottom of HNS
  OPEN: source and freshness of authorization/routing data.
  No accepted direct access to document PostgreSQL.
  No requirement to persist each live message before delivery.
end note
legend bottom
  Solid links: accepted direction; dotted link: open policy.
  A channel does not define delivery guarantees by itself.
  This view supersedes conflicting transport/ownership details in earlier sketches.
endlegend
@enduml
